      "explanation": "<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;max-height: 60vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 2 Online Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 30 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kzsh94dh/ccba9acc-8af6-42a1-b724-553c53746b2b/d19e7240-90c2-11ec-bd99-03b9d1656aa3/file-1kzsh94di.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>(a) If KNO<sub>2</sub> (Q)-on reacting with PhCH<sub>2</sub>Br(P) gives PhCH<sub>2</sub>ONO which on reduction with LiAlH<sub>4</sub> does not give PhCH<sub>2</sub>NH<sub>2</sub>.</p>\n\n<p>(b) If product R formed is benzylamine not benzene amine. KCN reacts with PhCH<sub>2</sub> Br to give PhCH<sub>2</sub>CN which does not have foul smelling.</p>\n\n<p>(c) If AgNO<sub>2</sub> (Q) reacts with PhCH<sub>2</sub> Br to give PhCH<sub>2</sub>NO<sub>2</sub>  which on reduciton give PhCH<sub>2</sub>NH<sub>2</sub><sub></sub> (Phenyl methanamine or benzyl amine).</p>\n\n<p>(d) If amide reacts with LiAlH 4 (W) to give amine. PhCH<sub>2</sub> Br reacts with AgCN to give PhCH<sub>2</sub>NO<sub>2</sub> .</p>"
